    <statement><p>The moose population on a small island is observed to be given by the function</p>
<p><me>P(t) = 120 t - 0.4 t^4 + 1100</me></p>
<p>where <m>t</m> is the time (in months) since observations of the island began.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/tests-applications-racoons-image-1.png" width="33%"/>
<p><alert> Note: </alert> you can get a larger view of the graph by clicking on it</p>
<p>(a) The maximum population attained at</p>
<p><m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> months.</p>
<p>The maximum population is</p>
<p><m>P(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> moose.</p>
<p>(b) When does the moose population disappear from the island?</p>
<p><m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/> months</p>
</statement>
